sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Router as OpenShift Router<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Gateway as Gateway (data-science-gateway)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS Terminate
    participant Envoy as Envoy Data Plane<br/>(Gateway)
    participant AuthProxy as kube-auth-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS (service-ca)
    participant OAuth as OAuth/OIDC Provider<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Component as Component Backend<br/>(via HTTPRoute)
    participant RBAC as kube-rbac-proxy sidecar<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant App as Application Container<br/>8080/TCP HTTP

    Note over Client,App: Flow 1: Client Request Through Gateway to Component

    Client->>Router: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+ (cluster ingress cert)
    Router->>Gateway: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS terminated at Gateway
    Gateway->>Envoy: Route to data plane

    Note over Envoy,AuthProxy: EnvoyFilter ext_authz check
    Envoy->>AuthProxy: HTTPS/8443<br/>TLS (service-ca cert)<br/>Authorization header check
    AuthProxy->>OAuth: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>OAuthClient credentials
    OAuth-->>AuthProxy: Token validation result
    AuthProxy-->>Envoy: Auth decision + user info

    Note over Envoy,Component: Lua filter: forward Bearer token, strip cookies
    Envoy->>Component: HTTP(S)/varies<br/>Bearer token via Authorization header
    Component->>RBAC: HTTPS/8443<br/>SubjectAccessReview
    RBAC->>App: HTTP/8080<br/>localhost (after RBAC check)
    App-->>RBAC: Response
    RBAC-->>Component: Response
    Component-->>Envoy: Response
    Envoy-->>Gateway: Response
    Gateway-->>Router: Response
    Router-->>Client: HTTPS Response

    Note over Client,App: Flow 2: Legacy Dashboard URL Redirect

    Client->>Router: HTTPS/443<br/>Route: rhods-dashboard<br/>TLS (edge termination)
    Router->>App: HTTP/8080<br/>dashboard-redirect Service
    App-->>Client: 301 Redirect to new Gateway hostname

    Note over Client,App: Flow 3: Component Provisioning (DSC Reconciliation)

    participant DSCCtrl as DSC Controller
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS

    DSCCtrl->>K8sAPI: Watch DataScienceCluster CR<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    K8sAPI-->>DSCCtrl: DSC spec (component states)
    DSCCtrl->>K8sAPI: Create Component CR<br/>(e.g., Dashboard, KServe)
    Note over DSCCtrl: Kustomize manifest rendering (local)
    DSCCtrl->>K8sAPI: SSA Apply manifests<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    K8sAPI-->>DSCCtrl: Apply result
